  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Density is people per square kilometre: population ÷ area.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Natural increase is births minus deaths; migration is added separately for total growth.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    A broad base means many births; a narrow apex means few survivors to old age.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Dependants (under 15 and over 64) are divided by the working-age group (15–64).
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Growth is the gap between the rates, and the gap is widest at the end of stage 2.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Push factors drive people away; jobs, schools and hospitals pull them in.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The direction of the move names the type: from the rural area to the urban one.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The measure is the share of the population in urban places, not the size of any one city.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    80 000 000 ÷ 400 000 = 200 people per km².
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Doubling time ≈ 70 ÷ growth rate = 70 ÷ 2 = 35 years.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Nearly half the population is under 15, so dependants outnumber workers.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The forest and derived savanna belts carry the densest rural populations, with Lagos the extreme.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Physical factors decide where farming is possible; economic factors decide where people concentrate.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The figure compares males with females; 102 means 102 boys for every 100 girls.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The balance of trade is an economic account, not a demographic measure.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    High fertility widens the base; developing countries in stage 2 show the classic expansive shape.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    It is the deaths of infants under one year, expressed per thousand live births.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    A census counts everyone, usually every ten years; a survey samples a part.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The 2006 count was 140 431 790; the 1991 count was 88.5 million.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The services that must expand with the population are the ones the growth strains.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    His claim was geometric population against arithmetic food, which is why he predicted checks.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    She held that scarcity of land pushes farmers to intensify and innovate.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Over-population is a relationship between numbers and resources, not an absolute figure.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Jobs, schools, hospitals and entertainment pull the young; the village offers few of them.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Emigration is outward; immigration is inward; internal migration is within.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Migrants send money home, and it is a major invisible earning for Nigeria.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The refugee's move is forced; the economic migrant's is chosen.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The world passed 8 billion in 2022.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    East and South Asia together hold the majority of humanity.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Many children and few workers mean the working group carries the cost of services.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    It is the average years of life expected at birth under current mortality.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    It is a lifetime average per woman, not a count of births in a year.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    About 2.4 per cent, which doubles the population in roughly thirty years.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The receiving city gains workers but strains housing, water, schools and transport.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    A pinched base means fewer births in recent years, so the birth rate has fallen.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The census is the primary source; the commission issues projections between counts.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    It tracks the two vital rates through four stages as a country develops.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The policy targets fertility, maternal health and the empowerment of women.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    A large old cohort is supported by a shrinking working group.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
